# SecureVoice AI — the names this project answers for on TLS.
#
# One name per line:  <hostname>  <address:port>
#
# The address is where this project's Caddy publishes 443 on the HOST's
# loopback, which is the value of CADDY_HTTPS_PORT in the host's .env. The
# front door runs in the host's network namespace, so it reaches the edge
# over 127.0.0.1 and nothing else — there is no Docker network shared with
# any product.
#
# The NAMES in this file are checked against the Caddyfile's own site list by
# tests/unit/edge-isolation.test.ts, so the front door and the edge cannot
# disagree about what this project serves. The PORT is checked against the
# running container by `bun scripts/deploy.mjs edge-status`.
#
# Format note: nginx's `map` reads the value as one token, so the address is
# written as address:port with no scheme and no path.
securevoiceai.me 127.0.0.1:8443
www.securevoiceai.me 127.0.0.1:8443
